     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I woke before the gulls to watch the sea\nGrey light pooling on the cold sand\nThe tide had left its night-writ lines\nIn foam and shell and broken strand\nA slow wave gathered far from shore\nAnd folded like a heavy door\nWhite spray hung a moment in the air\nThen vanished where the shallows tore\nThe wind came salted from the east\nIt lifted hair and coat and sail\nSmall boats leaned into its push\nTheir masts drew lines thin and pale\nI walked where water meets the land\nEach step erased by what came after\nThe ocean breathing in and out\nA deep lung full of light and laughter\nFar out a ship moved without sound\nA grey shape on a greyer line\nBetween the water and the sky\nIt hung, suspended out of time\nThe gulls cried sharp above the surf\nThey wheeled and fell and rose again\nHunting silver in the swell\nUnbothered by the coming rain\nThe clouds piled dark behind the headland\nThe sea turned green beneath their shade\nEach wave grew taller, louder, colder\nAs if by distant storms it was made\nI tasted salt upon my lips\nAnd felt the spray upon my face\nThe vastness calmed the noise in me\nAnd put my worries in their place\nNo road, no wall, no roof, no door\nCan hold the sea or make it stay\nIt gives and takes and takes and gives\nAnd wears the hardest stone away\nAt noon the sun broke through the grey\nAnd scattered gold across the blue\nThe water glittered, wide awake\nI left the shore, yet kept the sea with me\n",
      "state": {
       "itemId": "msg_01a1267d2bcc709ea98df620448b97cf"
      }
     }
